// CF-2 / t_79fc6bf7: a discard on the FALSE arm of a branch.
//
// The fragment that SURVIVES is the one that satisfied the condition, so
// the reference emits SGT and predicates the kill on EQ.  The default
// path recovers the guard as "the last comparison seen" - its block walk
// ignores the terminators - and emits the same SGT with the kill on NE:
// it kills exactly the fragments that must survive, silently, with a
// well-formed container and the right input mask.  Measured against the
// reference 2026-09-02; no shader in the corpus, the samples or the tests
// used this shape, which is why nothing caught it.
//
// The default path must REFUSE this until the matcher is retired
// (963018a's rule: an unrecognised shape refuses rather than mis-renders).
// The general path must compile it with the kill on EQ.
void main(float4 c : TEXCOORD0, out float4 o : COLOR)
{
    if (c.a > 0.5) {
        o = c;
    } else {
        discard;
    }
}
